&= 0 - \frac{1}{3} x^{-2/3}

\end{align}

{/eq}

Now, we can find the higher-order derivatives as follows:

{eq}\begin{align}

f''(x) &= \frac{d}{dx} f'(x)\\

&= \frac{d}{dx} 0 - \frac{1}{3} x^{-2/3}\\

&= -\frac{2}{3}x^{-5/3}

\end{align}

{/eq}

{eq}\begin{align}

f'''(x) &= \frac{d}{dx} f''(x)\\

&= -\frac{2}{3} \frac{d}{dx}x^{-5/3}\\

